WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Let's talk a little bit about what
exactly a commit is. Now,  we talked

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.940
about to commit being a snapshot and
that's exactly what it is. A commit  is

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.710
represented by a 40 character sha-1 hash and I wrote a couple little short versions

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:18.570
over here but in that 40 characters
there's a lot more than just numbers and

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:25.380
letters. There is a blob of the changes,
so blobs represent files, so you made

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.779
changes say to index.html, Git stores a
blob of that file which is a reduced

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:35.040
version of that code in a very
lightweight way. It also includes some

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.309
metadata. That means who made the
commit,

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:41.940
what time did they make the commit, and
what's the parent commit? Now what's the

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.020
commit that was made right before this
on this working branch. All that

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.460
information is stored and compressed in
that 40 characters sha-1 hash, which

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.699
means that commit ID is very, very
important.

